/*
 * The H.264 Start and Process commands' constant words for firmware 9013.55.1, as
 * macOS 27.2.1's VideoToolbox gives them to AppleAVE2 (a720, a360, a1080, a720b8, a720g2;
 * avetap, 2026-11-23), laid out as the 27.2 kext copies them into the commands.
 * Generated by tables9013.py from the capture: do not edit. Each run is its byte
 * offset in the command, its word count, its words.
 *
 * Start's regions, from S_AVE_UCInParam_Start's session settings ("ss"):
 *   +0x31f0 (0x5c0): settings, ss+0x0
 *   +0x37b0 (0x80): syntax configuration (_S_AVE_Syntax_Cfg_AVC), ss+0x1878
 *   +0x3830 (0x114): video parameters, ss+0x14a0
 * Process: P, AVE_PICMGMT_PARAMS, at +0xdc0: its first 0x1810 bytes the FrameInfo's
 * +0x5d28, the rest AVE_CHM_SetDataInfo_RC's and _Frame's copies of FrameInfo words.
 *
 * The kext's constant changes, applied:
 *   +0x35e8: settings+0x3f8 |= 0x10000: AVE_Work_Enc_TuneParam 0xfffffe0008f07480
 *   +0x382d: cfg+0x7d (client+0x2ea9) = 1: AVE_PSGen::Init; FW27 then builds its own SPS and PPS
 *   P+0x1824: client+0x2ec0 = 1: AVE_PSGen::Init, after Verify zeroed P+0x1810's source
 *   P+0x182c: client+0x2ec8 = 1: AVE_PSGen::Init
 *   P+0x1c1c: AVE_CHM_SetDataInfo_RC 0xfffffe0008dad738
 *
 * Left zero for the driver (ave-9013.c) to write:
 *   +0x322c: settings+0x3c: width
 *   +0x3230: settings+0x40: height, 16-aligned
 *   +0x32a0: settings+0xb0: height, 16-aligned
 *   +0x3600: settings+0x410: iFrameRate (K27 AVE_Client_Enc_Print)
 *   +0x3618: settings+0x428: bit rate, bit/s
 *   +0x36e8: settings+0x4f8: key frame interval
 *   +0x3760: settings+0x570: ThroughputMode (K27 AVE_Client_Enc_PrintAVC)
 *   +0x37b8: cfg+0x8: level, an index into FW27 AVC_FindLevelIdc's table
 *   +0x37d2: cfg+0x22, +0x24: width and height in macroblocks (u16)
 *   +0x3800: cfg+0x50: frame_cropping_flag
 *   +0x3802: cfg+0x52..+0x58: crop left, right, top, bottom (u16)
 *   0x4888: P+0x4888: width, height (FrameInfo+0x14f0, SetDataInfo_FwBuf 0xfffffe0008db7d9c)
 *   0x4890: P+0x4890: frame number (u64)
 *   0x49a0: P+0x49a0: time (u64), +0x49a8 timescale
 *   0x49f8: P+0x49f8: frame number (u64)
 */

